{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779066214,"nonce":"NauYFJnrr7iloMqCShkG5ED5GVQ=","title":"Phase 4c: run local Studio execution plans and attach artifacts","message":"## Parent / coordination\n- Roadmap: `fa3978f` — Feedbax/Mandible MVP integration roadmap.\n- Workspace foundation: `b424865`.\n- Execution-plan binding: `ddd3758`.\n- Pipeline workspace spec: `0c46f69`.\n- Provider/execution contract: `c6b1b73`.\n- Later full real-JAX training backend: `e57ae1f`.\n\n## Problem\nStudio can now prepare a provider-owned local execution plan from the active train-stage workspace scenario, but the plan is still only prepared/validated. The MVP needs one executable local path that writes the typed workspace/spec files, invokes the provider local execution boundary, and attaches emitted execution/manifests/artifacts back to the train stage. Without this, Studio state can still drift from the provider lineage model before cloud and full training runner slices arrive.\n\n## Scope\nImplement the next additive slice in a separate feature branch:\n- Add a backend-owned run path for a prepared Studio train-stage local execution.\n- Materialize `execution-spec.json`, `workspace-snapshot.json`, `graph-spec.json`, `training-spec.json`, and `task-spec.json` into the local run directory before launch.\n- Use the existing provider `run_local_execution` / `ExecutionSpec` boundary rather than a Studio-only shortcut.\n- Return an updated workspace with train-stage status, execution result, manifest refs, and artifact refs attached.\n- Add frontend API/store/UI wiring so Studio can run the prepared local execution and persist returned refs.\n- Preserve room for SSH, RunPod, Modal, eval, analysis, and report stages; do not bake training-only assumptions into the workspace model.\n\n## Non-goals\n- No live RunPod/Modal submission in this slice.\n- No full replacement of the stub/fake training worker with real JAX training; that remains `e57ae1f`.\n- No hidden frontend-only execution semantics.\n- No irreversible migration away from legacy project fields yet.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- A prepared local Studio train plan can be run through a Feedbax provider endpoint.\n- The run writes the expected spec snapshot files and emits a manifest-shaped local execution result.\n- The returned workspace carries execution result metadata, manifest refs, and artifact refs on the train stage.\n- Frontend state can store the returned result without dropping future/custom stage metadata.\n- Tests cover the backend run path and frontend store update behavior.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}